	(text "TI DN024 / SWRA227E meandering monopole, dual band 868 + 2440 MHz,\nlaid out the way the note's own Figure 2 lays it out.\n\nJ1 is P6: a vertical through-hole SMA jack, signal pin with four ground\nposts on a 5.08 mm square, sitting 22 mm inboard of the ground plane\nedge rather than on the board edge. Its drills are measured off Figure 2\nto about +/-0.1 mm - check them against the connector you buy.\n\nTable 3, dual band BOM:   Z61 NC   Z62 3.9 pF series   Z63 NC\n  -> measured SWR 1.2 at 868 MHz and 1.6 at 2.44 GHz\n\nThe top ground is cut away around the feed and the network, as Figure 2\ndraws it; the bottom ground stays solid and is what the 2.95 mm 50 ohm\nline is referenced to.\n\nEverything else - antenna, ground plane, clearances - is identical to\nthe dn024/ project, which uses an edge-launch SMA instead."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 112 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "68178ea6-bd39-5338-807b-afe2eaae2541")
	)
